1. Protect & Maintain What We Have\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Our parks, trails, open spaces, playgrounds, and facilities are valuable community assets. My priority is to protect that investment through responsible maintenance, long-term planning, and a strong commitment to safety. This will keep these resources safe, clean, and well maintained for today and future generations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Fiscal Responsibility & Accountable Leadership\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Every taxpayer dollar matters. I bring more than 20 years of experience working within this community, along with my School Board experience of overseeing budgets, contracts, risk management, and public resources. I understand the importance of planning for long-term maintenance, protecting existing assets, and understanding the financial impact before making new commitments.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Safety Through Strong Community Partnerships\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Safety requires agencies to work together. Through my service on the Tri-Agency Committee, I have firsthand experience working with the Park District, School District, City, and law enforcement on issues affecting our community. I will continue strengthening those relationships to help keep our parks, schools, trails, and recreational spaces safe.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Invest Wisely & Maximize Community Resources\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 I understand the Joint Use Agreements between the School District and Park District and how these partnerships help maximize facilities, programs, and taxpayer resources. We should continue sharing resources where it makes sense, avoiding unnecessary duplication, and making responsible investments that provide lasting value for children, families, adults, and seniors.}